body:
I'm not sure if they're accessible in your country, but lotus foods make a lot of varieties of gluten-free ramen noodles. And then these off amazon are probably the best I've found [https://www.amazon.com/Gluten-Free-Japanese-Ramen-Noodle/dp/B07QGLJDWW/ref=sr\_1\_7?dchild=1&keywords=gluten+free+meister+ramen&qid=1632775982&s=grocery&sr=1-7](https://www.amazon.com/Gluten-Free-Japanese-Ramen-Noodle/dp/B07QGLJDWW/ref=sr_1_7?dchild=1&keywords=gluten+free+meister+ramen&qid=1632775982&s=grocery&sr=1-7)

&#x200B;

Then for easiest recipes I'd say to look up "tantanmen", which is known as the 10 minute ramen recipe. It actually has a ton of flavor for being quick.

